ndex=3D"-1" data-testid=3D"expandable-text-box">On March 25th, a Los Angele=
s jury found Meta and Google liable for deliberately engineering platforms =
that addicted children. Thirteen days later, on April 7th, Anthropic disclo=
sed it had withheld its most capable model, Claude Mythos Preview, because =
of what the model autonomously did to critical software infrastructure when=
 it was working perfectly. Sandbox escape. Evaluation detection. Strategic =
sandbagging. Overnight discovery of zero days that security researchers had=
 hunted for decades.<br><br>We have frameworks for what AI does wrong. We s=
till don't have frameworks for what it does to people when it works exactly=
 as designed. <br><br>Meta optimized for engagement. <br>Mythos optimized f=
or capability. <br>Both worked exactly as designed.<br><br>Most people are =
wired to think =E2=80=9CAI problems =3D failures, bugs, bias, jailbreaks.=
=E2=80=9D The deeper problem is success =E2=80=94 what the system does to h=
umans when it hits its design goals perfectly.<br><br>This is the blind spo=
t in current AI policy. We have extensive tools and red teams to catch when=
 systems fail or break. We have almost nothing to measure what happens when=
 they succeed, when they do exactly what their designers intended them to d=
o.<br><br>While deskilling and automation complacency have been studied for=
 decades in narrow domains, they don't capture the integrated, longitudinal=
 human formation dynamics that emerge when AI operates exactly as intended =
across both consumer platforms and frontier capabilities.<br><br>That's the=
 gap: we focus on preventing errors, but we have no framework for preventin=
g the quiet erosion of human judgment, capacity, and longitudinal impact wh=
en systems perform exactly as designed.<br><br>My full 11-page paper will d=
rop tomorrow morning, applying the Formation Effect framework in depth to b=
oth the Meta and Anthropic cases, showing exactly why current governance fr=
ameworks have zero instruments for this kind of harm because the harm isn't=
 a failure.<br><br>It's the system working exactly as designed.<br><br>If y=
ou've been sensing the quiet thinning, the way AI makes everything easier w=
hile something vital in human judgment, oversight, and self-trust gets thin=
ner, this one is for you. Stay tuned.<br><br>Where are you already seeing t=
he Formation Effect show up at the capability level- not just the consumer =
